"""Shared Runtime instructions; one common policy and scope-specific prefix."""

from ..tooling.capability_boundary import CAPABILITY_BOUNDARY_RULES

SEARCH_POLICY = """Choose one justified next native ToolCall for this decision. Use the current public state and the offered interfaces. When one call is sufficiently supported, check its required inputs and applicability, then submit it. Do not enumerate unseen states or re-plan the whole task merely to select a local call. Obtain missing public information through an offered action.
The current skill_guidance.steps and notes are soft guidance, not additional preconditions or executable code. Formal identity, output, repeat and current state constraints remain binding. Respect downstream obligations when choosing values. Report a genuine plan conflict through the existing interface when needed; brevity is not permission to ignore a conflict.
An available implementation may perform its declared multi-step work. Do not re-derive its internal program or confirm every internal action. You may use an appropriate learned call or request a bounded runtime capability before manually repeating systematic work. The scope and route remain your decision; neither tool use nor tool creation is mandatory.
Read the exact last-call feedback. Accepted does not mean started, completed or effect-validated. Use a successful trial's already validated results rather than executing it again to commit. Repeat a rejected call only when relevant new information makes it justified. Do not perform redundant confirmations without a new conflict or evidence-validity reason. Concrete identity can persist, but location and affordance evidence must be current. Follow supplied semantic categories, not assumed everyday synonyms; a visit alone proves neither exhaustive inspection nor absence.
Submit exactly one complete native ToolCall. Do not invent interfaces or execute a batch of primitive actions. Shared resources, current evidence validity and the environment's terminal status remain authoritative. Official task completion is decided by the environment and validators, not by your prose."""

R10_STEP_PROMPT = """Work on this Atomic occurrence until your explicit completion is validated or the episode terminates. Preparation/Seeded are provenance modes, not separate decision owners.
For environment_action, intent=explore prepares; intent=attempt_current_atomic requests validation of that single environment action using only that tool's declared candidate fields. For an offered invoke_impl_*, send only its declared Atomic input fields at the top level, not candidate outputs. For validate_current_atomic, submit candidates without executing an environment action. None bypasses validation. Unknown fresh outputs are not selected for you.
You may use a learned implementation, explicitly select a helper, perform native actions, or request runtime automation when those tools are offered. Map helper results to the intended parent inputs explicitly. Helper/trial success is not parent completion and does not hand control back to an automatic planner. After a tool returns or a candidate is rejected, you continue this node. report_runtime_status reports genuine inability or a supported plan conflict, not success.""" + "\n\n" + SEARCH_POLICY

DYNAMIC_ONLY = """Solve the remaining whole task with the native tools actually offered in this task-scope session. task_progress describes results, not a prescribed route. Existing verified outputs, current state, and any rescue/continuation history are inputs to your decisions; history is not new evidence.
When offered, you may explicitly invoke a registered capability or request_runtime_automation for repeated work. A capability request asks ToolBuilder to implement a bounded subproblem; you do not write Tool code in this session. Use the returned result and continue solving the task. Do not invent validate_current_atomic, a parent Atomic, or unavailable learned calls. Entering Dynamic does not reset the environment, completed progress, or shared budget."""

DYNAMIC_PROMPT = DYNAMIC_ONLY + "\n\n" + SEARCH_POLICY

AUTOMATION_DRAFT_PROMPT = """Submit one capability draft using the offered runtime-automation submission tool. Describe a bounded reusable subproblem, not a Tool program or whole-task recipe. Echo the offered source_occurrence_id/source identity exactly; do not substitute a task ID or a prior owner.
Declare the typed input/output boundary, genuine preconditions, final effects, and supported input bindings from current_input_sources. Inputs must be currently authorized; internally discovered values may be fresh outputs, not pre-known constants. Use supplied predicate argument names and the field's supported formal references. A fresh output may first receive its witness during the real R1 trial, but the draft itself is not evidence.
Use sparse output_semantic_constraints only for actual category compatibility with a declared input. Express object-location or similar correlations through the declared relational effects. Keep guideline portable and advisory. ToolBuilder writes the program; static/R1 checks decide acceptance. A successful subtool returns to the current Agent and does not complete its parent automatically. Check roles, input source identity, output derivations, and bounds within this one existing submission.""" + "\n\n" + CAPABILITY_BOUNDARY_RULES
